            <div xml:id="d42-a1">

                <pb facs="0182" n="64" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg64"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    21.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Emperor’s abdication.</hi></head>
                <p>In view of the representation which was delivered to me to-day at 3 o’clock in
                    the afternoon, I resolve, yielding to the power of circumstances, to depart with
                    all my family for Europe to-morrow, leaving this country, beloved by us all, and
                    for which I have exerted myself to give constant proofs of deeply seated love,
                    and dedication for almost half a century, during which I filled the position of
                    chief of the state. In departing, therefore I with all the persons of my family,
                    shall always retain the most tender remembrances of Brazil in offering ardent
                    prayer for its greatness and prosperity.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">D. Pedro de Alcantara.</hi></signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1889-11-16"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 16,
                        1889</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
